.TE
.PP
The A/A difference of a cell lies between 0.07 and 10.9 percent (field
\f[CR]aa_percent\f[R] of the file).
The mbedded\-cbor sum reads each element through
\f[CR]i.at_path<\(dq\(at[]\(dq>()\f[R], not through the \f[CR]view\f[R]
of section 6.
.PP
bench/results has no measurement of nlohmann/json, libcbor, the plain
at_path form, the lazy elements form, structs, shared values or broken
input against another library in this image.
This document gives no number for them.
.SS 10. Other decoders read what mbedded\-cbor writes
\f[CR]test/interop/run.sh\f[R] writes values with every public writer:
\f[CR]cbor::encoder\f[R], \f[CR]cbor::encode(item)\f[R],
\f[CR]structs<T>::encode\f[R] and \f[CR]schema<T>::encode\f[R].
The values are the examples of RFC 8949 Appendix A, the cbor\-wg test
vectors, the bench corpora, every integer and float width, tags 28 and
29, and typed arrays.
Each decoder below reads the output.
The script then compares the value with the value that was written.
\f[CR]test/run.sh full\f[R] runs it, and the CI runs it at each push.
The decoders are the packages of Debian sid.
